    "intro_html":  "Meatballs on a sheet pan are one of the great meal prep discoveries. No frying, no splatter, no standing at the stove turning them one at a time. They roast alongside pineapple, onion and red pepper, everything gets glazed in barbecue sauce, and it all goes over rice. Each serving lands at {{cal}} calories with \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). Canned pineapple caramelizing next to barbecue sauce is a flavor combination that has never lost an argument.",
